null,"state":"OH"},{"bioguideId":"B001324","fullName":"Rep. Bell, Wesley [D-MO-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-21","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MO"},{"bioguideId":"C001069","fullName":"Rep. Courtney, Joe [D-CT-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-06-25","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CT"},{"bioguideId":"F000454","fullName":"Rep. Foster, Bill [D-IL-11]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-07-02","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IL"},{"bioguideId":"D000399","fullName":"Rep. Doggett, Lloyd [D-TX-37]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-08-12","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"C001119","fullName":"Rep. Craig, Angie [D-MN-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-15","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MN"},{"bioguideId":"H001047","fullName":"Rep. Himes, James A. [D-CT-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CT"},{"bioguideId":"W000831","fullName":"Rep. Walkinshaw, James R. [D-VA-11]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-21","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-20T14:10:13+00:00","id":"hr1674-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-27","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-02-27","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"laws":[],"number":"1674","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"D000197","district":1,"fullName":"Rep. DeGette, Diana [D-CO-1]","party":"D","state":"CO"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-02-27","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><b>Keep Americans Safe Act</b></p> <p>This bill establishes a new criminal offense for the import, sale, manufacture, transfer, or possession of a large capacity ammunition feeding device (LCAFD).</p> <p>The bill does not prohibit certain conduct with respect to an LCAFD, including the following:</p> <ul> <li> importation, sale, manufacture, transfer, or possession related to certain law enforcement efforts, or authorized tests or experiments;</li> <li>importation, sale, transfer, or possession related to securing nuclear materials; and</li> <li> possession by a retired law enforcement officer.</li> </ul> <p>The bill permits continued possession of, but prohibits sale or transfer of, a grandfathered LCAFD.</p> <p>Newly manufactured LCAFDs must display serial number identification and the date of manufacture.</p> <p> Additionally, the bill allows a state or local government to use Edward Byrne Memorial Justice Assistance Grant Program funds to compensate individuals who surrender an LCAFD under a buy-back program.</p>","updateDate":"2026-02-19T19:58:28Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Keep Americans Safe Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:19:19Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:19:19Z"}
